<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb gold imports down 18.0 pct yr/yr--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan Feb gold imports down 18.0 pct yr/yr--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's gold imports in February fell by 18.0 percent from a year earlier to 14.49 tonnes, Finance Ministry data released on Friday showed.</p>
<p>The figures were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			  Feb 97    Jan 97    Feb 96</p>
<p> Total		  14.49     11.50	17.67</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> South Africa	  5.88	3.16	 2.63</p>
<p> Switzerland	   3.54	1.38	 2.62</p>
<p> Australia	     2.23	2.25	 4.91</p>
<p> Britain		 0.50	0.50	 2.61</p>
<p> South Korea	   1.30	1.30	 1.35</p>
<p>Cumulative gold imports in the first two months of 1997 totalled 25.99 tonnes, down from 30.79 tonnes in the same period a year earlier year.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3 3432 7431</p>
</text>
